   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How it is formed",
     "texto": [
      "In **-are** and **-ere** verbs, the conditional stem usually ends in **-er-**: **parlare → parlerei**, **prendere → prenderei**. In **-ire** verbs it keeps **-ir-**: **dormire → dormirei**. The endings are **-ei, -esti, -ebbe, -emmo, -este, -ebbero**.",
      "Some verbs are irregular in the stem: **avere → avrei**, **essere → sarei**, **andare → andrei**, **fare → farei**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs of wishing",
     "texto": [
      "**Vorrei** (I would like), **potrei** (I could), **dovrei** (I should), **mi piacerebbe** (I would like).",
      "With **mi piacerebbe** the thing that would be liked goes afterwards: **Mi piacerebbe un viaggio** (I would like a trip)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
